From 0c4b8801e253e98aa179afc13e3c1650026ebe7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wasabipesto-bot <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] exp: NICE_EXP_GPU_PROFILE per-phase join profile; harness
 size/starts knobs

Experimental instrumentation for the research program (L1), not for merge.

- NICE_EXP_GPU_PROFILE=1 synchronises the device after each kernel group
  of every join batch (inputs, top/top_scan/top_fill, bucket, join, check)
  and around JoinDevice::new and the reads, and prints one GPU_PROFILE line
  per field: seconds per phase, top-layer prefixes, bpre entries, certified
  tops, listed bottom entries, AND pairs (raw and wave-padded), live
  buckets, AND survivors, prefilter survivors, hits. Unset, nothing runs.
- Throughput harness: NICE_TEST_JOIN_SIZE (default 1e14, warm-up stays at
  most 1e14), NICE_TEST_JOIN_STARTS=b:start overrides, and starts for b58
  (the b58_msd_weak field) and b62 (PLAN_FIELDS).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
